  "content": "<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>\n<multiple-choice question=\"What is the main purpose of render passes (AOVs)?\" single-option=\"\" randomize=\"\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"To output separate components, such as diffuse, specular and shadows, for compositing\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"To render faster at lower quality\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"To save the image in several file formats\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"To preview the scene in the viewport\">\n</multiple-choice>\n<true-false-question question=\"In a path tracer, raising the sample count usually reduces noise but increases render time.\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"True\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"False\">\n</true-false-question>\n<self-check title=\"Think it through\">\n  <p slot=\"question\">Your render takes too long. Name three changes that would shorten it, and what each one costs.</p>\n  <p>For example: fewer samples with a denoiser (can lose fine detail), fewer light bounces (less realistic indirect light), a lower resolution or render region (less image), or simpler geometry and smaller textures (less detail). Adaptive sampling and GPU rendering can also help.</p>\n</self-check>\n"
}